## Summary

| Concept | Key Takeaway |
|---|---|
| **Foundry Project Init** | Use `forge init` to create a project; delete default files to build from scratch |
| **Factory Contract** | A globally unique registry responsible for deploying and recording all Pair contracts |
| **Pair Contract** | Independently deployed per trading pair; handles fund custody and trade execution; also serves as an ERC20 (LP Token) |
| **Nested Mapping** | `mapping(address => mapping(address => address))` enables dual-key lookup |
| **Address Sorting** | A ternary expression ensures `token0 < token1`, preventing duplicate pool creation |

**Key Takeaway for Today**: Uniswap V2 employs a **Factory + Pair** factory pattern. The Factory is responsible for creating and registering trading pairs, while the Pair handles actual fund management and trade execution. To guarantee that each token pair has only one liquidity pool, the system uses a nested mapping for storage and canonicalizes input through address sorting to eliminate ambiguity from different input orders. This lean yet elegant architecture is the cornerstone for understanding the entire Uniswap V2 protocol.
